{"name":"Graphic Charcoal","hex":"#5c5e5f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"graphic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Drawn, pictorial.","Explicit, vivid, descriptive, often in relation to depictions of sex or violence."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A drawing or picture.","A computer-generated image as viewed on a screen forming part of a game or a film etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/graphic"},{"term":"charcoal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["impure carbon obtained by destructive distillation of wood or other organic matter, that is, heating it in the absence of oxygen.","A stick of black carbon material used for drawing."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a dark gray colour.","Made of charcoal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/charcoal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Graphics","blocks":[{"text":"Graphics are visual images or designs on some surface, such as a wall, canvas, screen, paper, or stone, to inform, illustrate, or entertain. In contemporary usage, it includes a pictorial representation of data, as in design and manufacture, in typesetting and the graphic arts, and in educational and recreational software. Images that are generated by a computer are called computer graphics."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Graphics","wikidata":"Q1027879"},{"title":"Charcoal","blocks":[{"text":"Charcoal is a lightweight black residue made of carbon that is produced by strongly heating wood in minimal oxygen to remove all water and volatile constituents. In the traditional version of this pyrolysis process, called charcoal burning, often by forming a charcoal kiln, the heat is supplied by burning part of the starting material itself, with a limited supply of oxygen. The material can also be heated in a closed retort. Modern charcoal briquettes used for outdoor cooking may contain many other additives, e.g. coal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Charcoal_8.jpg/330px-Charcoal_8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charcoal","wikidata":"Q177463"},{"title":"Shades of gray","blocks":[{"text":"Variations of gray or grey include achromatic grayscale shades, which lie exactly between white and black, and nearby colors with low colorfulness. A selection of a number of these various colors is shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Shades_of_Gray.svg/330px-Shades_of_Gray.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_gray","wikidata":"Q3958716"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Leonardo_da_Vinci_-_presumed_self-portrait_-_WGA12798.jpg/500px-Leonardo_da_Vinci_-_presumed_self-portrait_-_WGA12798.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Leonardo_da_Vinci_-_presumed_self-portrait_-_WGA12798.jpg/1280px-Leonardo_da_Vinci_-_presumed_self-portrait_-_WGA12798.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Leonardo_da_Vinci_-_presumed_self-portrait_-_WGA12798.jpg/500px-Leonardo_da_Vinci_-_presumed_self-portrait_-_WGA12798.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Example of a drawing. This portrait was drawn by Leonardo da Vinci around 1510, and it might depict the artist himself. It is executed in Sanguine (a kind of red chalk) on paper.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALeonardo_da_Vinci_-_presumed_self-portrait_-_WGA12798.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Tulip01.jpg/500px-Tulip01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikiped